---
/* Rendered only on a page in draft mode (staging or development; production
   never is): a small label saying the page shows unpublished drafts, with the
   way out of draft mode. Shown in a normal browser tab only; inside the
   Studio's Visual editor, which has its own controls, it stays hidden. Its
   style and script are inline, so no build carries them unless it is shown. */
---
<aside class="draft-mode-label" data-draft-mode-label hidden>
  <span>[&nbsp;Drafts&nbsp;]</span>
  <a href="/api/draft-mode/disable" data-barba-prevent="self">Exit</a>
</aside>
<style is:inline>
  .draft-mode-label {
    position: fixed;
    left: 1.6rem;
    bottom: 1.6rem;
    z-index: 1000; /* above the site's own layers (400 at most) */
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.24);
    background: #000;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--size-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .draft-mode-label[hidden] { display: none; }
  .draft-mode-label a { color: #e6402a; }
</style>
<script is:inline>
  if (window.self === window.top) document.querySelector('[data-draft-mode-label]').hidden = false;
</script>
